{
  "comment": "CDP methods the oko bridge may relay to a handed-over tab. Both sides enforce it: the bridge for its clients, the extension for the bridge. 'client' is what oko commands may call; 'bridge' is what the bridge itself sends (frame auto-attach, undo, idle clean-up). Anything else - cookies, Storage, Target, Browser, Tracing, IO, Fetch, SystemInfo - is refused. Page.navigate is further limited to http(s) and about:blank.",
